	</span>
</h2>
<p>Today, we're announcing <strong>Qwen3-Coder-Next</strong>, an open-weigh=
t language model designed specifically for coding agents and local developm=
ent. It features the following key enhancements:  </p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Super Efficient with Significant Performance</strong>: With onl=
y 3B activated parameters (80B total parameters), it achieves performance c=
omparable to models with 10=E2=80=9320x more active parameters, making it h=
ighly cost-effective for agent deployment.</li>
<li><strong>Advanced Agentic Capabilities</strong>: Through an elaborate tr=
aining recipe, it excels at long-horizon reasoning, complex tool usage, and=
 recovery from execution failures, ensuring robust performance in dynamic c=
oding tasks.</li>
<li><strong>Versatile Integration with Real-World IDE</strong>: Its 256k co=
ntext length, combined with adaptability to various scaffold templates, ena=
bles seamless integration with different CLI/IDE platforms (e.g., Claude Co=
de, Qwen Code, Qoder, Kilo, Trae, Cline, etc.), supporting diverse developm=
ent environments.</li>
</ul>
